Spec: TenantContextScript

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  The tenant-kind context orchestrator: structural twin of ./../service/context.rhai
    (./../service/context.sdd) one level above @build_context, turning the assembled
    map into the tenant contract the install/delete/template lanes consume. Same
    skeleton as the twin — delegate, overlay `template_dir`/`agent_image`, guarded
    hook slots — with four deltas: it mints `tenant` (not `namespace`) with
    maintenance hour `"1"`; the kind slot is `context_tenant` (not
    `context_service`); the live lane does cluster reads of its own (the tenant
    identity getters plus one per-namespace @TenantInstance list for the published
    services) inline right after the mint; and the offline lane has no
    `context_after` slot (the twin calls it on both).

Exposes:
  @run(@instance, @args) — live lane, the entry point the agent tenant `install`
    and `delete` snippets call via `ctx::run(instance, args)`
    (/agent/src/tenant/install.sdd, /agent/src/tenant/delete.sdd; also the
    @ENTRY_POINT_FUNCTIONS lint name `run` of /agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.sdd);
    delegates to `build::run`, hooks through the three-arg @import_run.
  @template(@instance, @args) — offline twin for `agent template tenant`:
    delegates to `build::template`, hooks through @import_template, one slot
    shorter (no `context_after`).
  No other @fn exists — importing this module (alias convention `as ctx`, also
    under the package-shadow name `context`) exposes exactly these two.

Accepts:
  @instance — NOT forwarded blind here (twin delta): typed @TenantInstance @Dynamic
    fetched by @TenantInstance::get before the eval (/agent/src/tenant/install.sdd,
    /agent/src/tenant/delete.sdd), the synthesized `#{metadata: {name, namespace}}`
    map of /agent/src/template/tenant.sdd, or the mock-sink value of
    @get_tenant_instance under `agent package test` (/agent/src/testing/handler.sdd).
    The `template` lane reads `metadata.namespace` inside the mint; the `run` lane
    calls the registered `get_tenant_name` and `get_tenant_namespaces` bridges
    (/common/src/instancetenant.sdd).
  @args — plain map: the caller's serialized @Parameters (install lane ten
    snake_case keys, delete lane nine — NO `tag`, so `instance.requested` lands as
    `()` upstream). Keys THIS file reads, ungated: `template_dir` (serialized
    @PathBuf text) and `agent_image` (@common::DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE-backed default);
    a missing key lands `()`. Everything else is consumed downstream through the
    delegation and the hooks (read contract ./../lib/build_context.sdd and
    ./context_tenant.sdd).

Returns:
  The context map (last expression; the calling snippet passes it to
    `install::run`/`delete::run`/`template::run`, the Rust lane discards the
    snippet @Dynamic). Both lanes, insertion order of top-level keys:
    1. the delegate's seven (`cluster`, `controller`, `instance`, `values`,
        `defaults`, `package_dir`, `config_dir` — key contract owned there),
    2. `template_dir` then `agent_image` — verbatim copies of the args values,
    3. whatever the `context_pre` replacement leaves (whole-map replacement can
        rewrite or erase every key above),
    4. `tenant` — run lane: a map with `name` from `get_tenant_name()`,
        `namespaces` from `get_tenant_namespaces()`, a gathered `services`
        array and the maintenance pair `maintenance_start_hour: "1"` plus
        `maintenance_start_minut: "0"`; template lane: the placeholder block
        with `name: "client"`, `namespaces` `["client-system", instance.metadata.namespace]`
        (literal previews), the same maintenance pair and NO `services` key
        at all (frozen upstream by /agent/src/template/tenant.sdd);
        overwrites anything `context_pre` wrote under `tenant`,
    5. whatever the shipped `context_tenant` slot leaves — its aliasing of
        `namespace` onto the same map and the added `use_backup`/`ha`/`name`
        and annotation-derived keys are owned by ./context_tenant.sdd,
    6. `extra` — always written to the `context_extra` result, no guard; the stock
        image (no such module ships) stores `()`.
  run lane only, last: whatever `context_post` then `context_after` replacements
    leave. template lane: `context_post` is the last slot — `context_after` is
    never resolved offline (twin asymmetry, Tasks).
  Later stage modules of the same run add keys (e.g. ./install_tofu.rhai's
    `tofu`); that is their contract.

Raises:
  Zero @throw in this file; its only @try is per-namespace inside the live gather.
    - Delegation errors land whole (package.yaml read, agent.yaml YAML, unguarded
      cluster reads per ./../lib/build_context.sdd Raises).
    - `instance.get_tenant_name()` is unguarded: its Rhai bridge propagates the
      failure (@rhai::EvalAltResult per /common/src/instancetenant.sdd Raises) and
      aborts the live lane before the `tenant` key exists.
    - `instance.get_tenant_namespaces()` swallows cluster failures upstream into the
      plain string `""` (frozen in /common/src/instancetenant.sdd Tasks):
      `tenant.namespaces` then stores a string, the gather loop iterates zero
      times, `services` stays `[]` and no log line is emitted here.
    - Gather failures (the per-namespace `TenantInstance` list, the property walks,
      the `service` flatten): caught per namespace — @log_warn of the string as-is
      or @json_encode of anything else — that namespace stops, the next keeps
      going, entries already pushed in `tenant.services` stay.
    - Hook errors: @import_run/@import_template swallow ONLY absent-module /
      absent-function (skip with @log_debug, semantics owned by vynil-core
      @add_common); anything a hook throws for real propagates and aborts the lane.

Handles:
  Stock image hook posture: only `context_tenant` ships (this directory);
    `context_pre`/`context_extra`/`context_post`/`context_after` skip on every lane
    to `()`, so the guards keep the running context and only `extra` changes (to
    `()`).
  Non-map hook return (including the skip `()`) silently keeps the previous
    context — guard `type_of(ctx) == "map"`, whole-value replacement, no merge.
  @import_template fallback: a hook module without `template` but with `run` is
    invoked at `run(instance, context)` offline — a run-only package hook executes
    its cluster reads during `agent template`.
  Gather shape guard: a @TenantInstance whose `status` is not a map or whose
    `status.services` is not an array is skipped silently (its records contribute
    nothing, no log).
  Gather entries are the serialized @crate::Published records — the `service` field
    serializes as `null` when absent (no skip), so the `"service" in s` guard passes
    and `s += s.service` sees a non-map (Tasks).
  Package shadow resolution: resolver order `{package_dir}/scripts`,
    `{config_dir}`, `{script_dir}/tenant`, `{script_dir}/lib` — a package
    `context.rhai` replaces this orchestrator, `context_tenant.rhai` the kind
    slot, `build_context.rhai` the delegate.

Must:
  Keep the module body at one plain `import "build_context" as build` plus the two
    `fn` declarations — nothing runs at import; both entry names match
    @ENTRY_POINT_FUNCTIONS.
  Run each lane in this order, every guarded slot exactly once: delegate, then
    `context["template_dir"]`/`context["agent_image"]` copies, then slot
    `context_pre`, then [live only] `get_tenant_name()` and
    `get_tenant_namespaces()` on the instance, then mint `tenant`, then [live
    only] the services gather, then slot `context_tenant`, then write `extra`
    from slot `context_extra`, then slot `context_post`, then [live only] slot
    `context_after`, then return `context`.
  Gather services between the mint and the `context_tenant` slot: for each
    namespace of the list, one @k8s_resource @list of kind `TenantInstance`
    scoped to that namespace (not a cluster sweep), and push one entry per
    `status.services` member, each enriched with an `instance` map
    `#{name, namespace}` of the
    owner @TenantInstance and a `package` map carrying `category` from
    `spec.category` and `name` from `spec["package"]`, and its `service`
    payload flattened into the entry
    (`s += s.service` then @remove) when the `service` key is there, in
    namespace-list then status order. No filter and no dedup: the calling
    instance's own published services are included and the record's `tenant` tag
    key SURVIVES on the entry (unlike @build_context's filtered `cluster.services`);
    the same service can therefore appear under both keys of the map.
  Replace on the guarded slots through `type_of(ctx) == "map"`, whole map, no key
    merge; store the `context_extra` result into `extra` unguarded (any value,
    including `()`, becomes the stored value).
  Mint `tenant` AFTER `context_pre` and BEFORE `context_tenant`: the kind slot
    must see the minted map (it reads and extends it), and `context_pre` has no
    way to seed `tenant` — its map under that key is overwritten.
  Mint the maintenance pair as the strings `maintenance_start_hour: "1"` and
    `maintenance_start_minut: "0"` on both lanes (service twin uses hour `"0"`,
    Tasks); the `minut` misspelling is load-bearing —
    ./../lib/backup_context.rhai builds the cron `schedule` from
    `namespace.maintenance_start_minut`/`maintenance_start_hour`.
  Preserve the key spellings `template_dir`, `agent_image`, `tenant`, `services`,
    `namespaces`, `extra` and the maintenance pair verbatim — the downstream
    indexers are ./schedule_backup.rhai, ./init_from.rhai, ./delete_vitals.rhai
    and ./restore_secret.rhai (@register_partial_dir of `context.template_dir` as
    the hbs partial root), ./../lib/backup_context.rhai (Job env value
    `context.agent_image`, `namespace.ha` replica count, the cron pair),
    ./../lib/tofu_gen.rhai (renders `extra` into the `vynil_extra` local),
    ./install.rhai (`context.namespace.use_backup`) and ./schedule_backup.rhai
    (`context.tenant.namespaces` install-allowlist check).

Must not:
  Serve the backup/restore lanes: the tenant `backup`/`restore` commands import
    ./backup.rhai / ./restore.rhai, which build their own map via
    ./../lib/backup_context.rhai @from_args and never import `context` — same
    directory, adjacent names, wrong contract.
  Validate or interpret `template_dir`/`agent_image` before storing them.

Depends on:
  ./../lib/build_context.rhai — the whole delegation (frozen there; only the seam —
    call once, per lane, first — is this file's contract).
  ./context_tenant.rhai — the shipped `context_tenant` slot; slot placement only
    here, internals in ./context_tenant.sdd.
  /common/src/instancetenant.sdd — the registered `get_tenant_name` /
    `get_tenant_namespaces` bridges this file calls on @instance (including the
    raise-vs-`""` asymmetry frozen in its Tasks).
  vynil-core 0.7.7 script surface (@Script `add_common` behind
    /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd): three-arg @import_run/@import_template,
    @type_of, @k8s_resource(...).@list, @json_encode, @log_warn, plain module
    `import` name resolution.
  Counterpart contracts, call edges flow the other way (they import this module):
    /agent/src/tenant/install.sdd and /agent/src/tenant/delete.sdd (live
    `ctx::run`), /agent/src/template/tenant.sdd (offline `ctx::template`),
    /agent/src/testing/handler.sdd (mock-engine lane of `agent package test`).

References:
  ./context_tenant.sdd — co-authored this pass; the `namespace` alias and
    annotation overlay in Returns.
  ./../service/context.sdd — the calibration twin. Its twin paragraph in
    References claims the twins mint no `template_dir`/`agent_image`: FALSE — this
    file copies both on both lanes; its "call `context_after` only on the live
    lane" claim about the tenant twin is true.
  /agent/src/template/tenant.sdd — offline lane freezing this file's outcome from
    its side (placeholder tenant block, stop at `context_post`).
  /agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.sdd — the `run`/`template` entry-name lint.

Scenario: live lane mints tenant identity and gathers published services
  Given a mock engine where `get_tenant_name` answers `acme`,
    `get_tenant_namespaces` answers `["team-a", "team-b"]`, `team-a` holds two
    @TenantInstances — one with a two-record `status.services` (both records
    carrying a `service` payload), one with no status at all — and `team-b` holds
    one record
  When @run(@instance, @args) executes
  Then `tenant.name` is `acme`, `tenant.namespaces` the two-element list,
    `tenant.maintenance_start_hour` the string `1`, and `tenant.services` holds
    the three records in namespace then status order, each with the owner
    `instance` and `package` submaps attached and the fqdn/port payload flattened,
    the statusless instance skipped silently
  No mapped test

Scenario: one namespace failing does not stop the gather
  Given the `TenantInstance` @list of the second namespace raises
  When the loop continues
  Then @log_warn carries the error text, that namespace contributes no entries,
    the remaining namespaces still iterate and entries pushed earlier stay in
    `tenant.services`
  No mapped test

Scenario: swallowed namespace getter lands a string
  Given `get_tenant_namespaces` returns the plain string `""` because the upstream
    bridge swallowed a cluster failure
  When @run continues
  Then `tenant.namespaces` is that string, the gather loop iterates zero times,
    `services` stays `[]` and this file logs nothing; while a failing
    `get_tenant_name` instead aborts the whole lane before `tenant` exists
  No mapped test

Scenario: a hook returning a map replaces everything
  Given a package `context_pre` hook whose `run` returns `#{only: 1}`
  When the first guarded slot takes it
  Then the context is `#{only: 1}`, and this file still writes `tenant` and
    `extra` onto it — later readers of erased delegate keys get `()` downstream,
    and the shipped `context_tenant` slot aborts the lane on the interpreter error
    for its erased `cluster`/`tenant` reads
  No mapped test

Scenario: offline lane mints the placeholder and stops at context_post
  Given the /agent/src/template/tenant.sdd synthesized instance with namespace
    `team-a`
  When @template(@instance, @args) executes
  Then `tenant` lands literally as name `client` with namespaces
    `["client-system", "team-a"]`, maintenance `1`/`0`, no `services` key; the guardless `context_post`
    is the last import and a package `context_after` hook is never resolved
    offline; the return is the map after `extra`
  No mapped test

Scenario: extra stores the raw slot result
  Given a package `context_extra` module returning `#{tools: []}` — or no such
    module
  When the slot writes `context["extra"]`
  Then the stored value is the raw return (or `()`) with no guard, and the tofu
    lane renders it as the `vynil_extra` local
  No mapped test

Tasks:
  [ ] Map the scenarios with tests: no tenant Rhai lane test exists —
      /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs only builds service engines
      (`scripts/service` + `scripts/lib`); add a tenant resolver builder (plus a
      fixture packages dir so hook shadowing is testable) before the TTD green
      gate.
  [ ] Verify `agent package test` actually drives @run for a tenant fixture (the
      mock instance must back the registered `get_tenant_name` /
      `get_tenant_namespaces` names per /agent/src/testing/handler.sdd) and fold
      the result into the coverage task above.
  [?] Maintenance hour `"1"` vs the service twin's `"0"`: a deliberate offset
      maintenance window or copy drift — decide/confirm. The pair is read by
      nobody in this directory's ./maintenance_start.rhai /
      ./maintenance_stop.rhai stubs, only via ./../lib/backup_context.rhai.
  [?] Placeholder previews: template-lane `client`/`client-system` misdescribe a
      real tenant; decision already open in
      /agent/src/template/tenant.sdd — mirror the outcome here.
  [?] Whole-gather unfiltered: own services included, `tenant` tag kept, and
      duplicates vs @build_context's separately-filtered `cluster.services`
      possible — confirm intent or mirror that filter.
  [?] Null payload flatten: @Published serializes `service: null`
      unconditionally, so `"service" in s` is always true and `s += s.service`
      on a payloadless record likely raises into the per-namespace
      catch, silently losing that namespace's later entries — pin the engine
      behavior with a test, then decide whether to guard the payload type.
  [?] `context_after` missing from the template lane (live-only slot): same
      asymmetry flagged in /agent/src/template/tenant.sdd — decide whether
      "after" must also fire offline or document why not.
  [?] `extra` unguarded and whole-map replacement semantics: same open twin
      decisions as ./../service/context.sdd Tasks.
  [?] The twin paragraph of ./../service/context.sdd misstates this file
      (claims no `template_dir`/`agent_image` mint here) — correct it under that
      spec's authority in a later pass.

Done when:
  Every Scenario has a mapped mock-engine test or decided Task, the twin-diff and
    key spellings cross-check against ./../service/context.sdd,
    ./../lib/build_context.sdd and ./context_tenant.sdd, and `specdd lint` is
    green.
